    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Perplexity Sonar is an API only family, so there are no open weights to download or self host, and every version is reached through a provider. Across all 5 versions, 3 support reasoning and none publish open weights, with context windows from 127072 to 200000 tokens. Input can include images alongside text, and output is text. The spread of versions matters for cost and output room. The cheapest tier, Sonar, is $1 per million input and $1 output with a max output of 114364 tokens, while Sonar Pro and Sonar Pro Search cost $3 input and $15 output with only 8000 max output tokens. The reasoning tiers, Sonar Reasoning Pro and Sonar Deep Research, sit at $2 input and $8 output with 115200 max output tokens. This suggests the family suits hosted search and research style tasks where long inputs and reasoning help, but limits appear when large outputs are needed on the pricier Pro tiers, and costs rise sharply for high volume use.",
